WEBVTT

00:00:08,850 --> 00:00:15,570
You say that we should not take glutathione supplements if we have cancer, but is it okay to take

00:00:15,570 --> 00:00:21,090
NAC to help boost our glutathione levels naturally, or is it defeating the purpose?

00:00:22,610 --> 00:00:29,010
If a person is in full remission of their cancer, I don't think they have any trouble taking

00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:42,130
NAC. So, NAC is what NAC is. And NAC is the precursors to glutathione. So normally, in the mitochondria,

00:00:42,130 --> 00:00:50,850
glutathione is recycled. That's how it works. That's how important glutathione is as the main

00:00:51,810 --> 00:01:01,570
this main antioxidant of a cell. So, in the cell, you have mitochondria and they're making glutathione

00:01:01,570 --> 00:01:08,530
and recycling glutathione, and they need cysteine and glycine as components to help with that

00:01:08,530 --> 00:01:17,570
recycling process and magnesium and some other cofactors. So, NAC is typically given to help boost

00:01:17,570 --> 00:01:25,650
glutathione levels. Now, if a person has is in kind of full-blown cancer, then I'd say no, you

00:01:25,650 --> 00:01:35,010
shouldn't be adding too much anesthetal cysteine to the system unless it's testifying for that person,

00:01:35,010 --> 00:01:40,610
but it typically would not. And you certainly wouldn't take like a glutathione, or the

00:01:40,690 --> 00:01:45,330
like was able glutathione supplement if you have cancer. But if you're in remission,

00:01:48,050 --> 00:01:57,890
helping with glutathione precursors, which NAC is, could help, you're not dealing with active

00:01:57,890 --> 00:02:02,050
cancer that I'd say it's okay to take. But if you're dealing with active cancer, I'd say maybe

00:02:02,050 --> 00:02:03,650
hold off on that.

